Pursuant to Section 4(b) of the Apache License 2.0, the following files contain
modifications from the original work:

  SKILL.md
      Rewritten. The original project ships a Python/LangGraph implementation;
      this file is a natural-language re-specification of the same agent graph
      for execution inside a single-model agent runtime.

  references/roles.md
      Rewritten from the original agent prompt modules under
      tradingagents/agents/ (analysts, researchers, risk_mgmt, trader,
      managers). Changes:
        - Technical/market analyst demoted from a peer analyst to an execution
          appendix; all directional calls removed from its mandate.
        - Fundamental analyst gains a "deviation vs consensus/guidance" section.
        - Sentiment analyst now must deliver hard sell-side consensus numbers.
        - Research manager and portfolio manager must respond to the
          implied-expectations file (pricing.md) and name the specific
          consensus assumption they disagree with.
        - Data sources changed from yfinance / SEC EDGAR / FRED / StockTwits /
          Reddit to public retrieval plus official filings; China A-share and
          Hong Kong sentiment sources changed to Xueqiu / Guba / Eastmoney.

  references/report-template.md
  references/data-checklist.md
  references/memory-protocol.md
      New files. The original project has no report template, no data checklist
      and no written memory protocol.

  scripts/init_run.py
  scripts/build_report.py
  scripts/implied.py
      New files. Zero-dependency Python standard library only. The original
      project's reporting and reflection logic lives inside its Python package
      and is not reused here.

  examples/
      New. Output produced by this workflow on CRWD as of 2026-10-22, included
      to document the expected report shape.

The following mechanisms are adapted from the original work:

  - The four-analyst / bull-bear debate / research manager / trader /
    three-way risk debate / portfolio manager topology, as implemented in
    tradingagents/graph/setup.py.
  - Debate turn routing, as implemented in
    tradingagents/graph/conditional_logic.py.
  - The five-tier rating vocabulary (Buy / Overweight / Hold / Underweight /
    Sell) and its regex parsing, as implemented in tradingagents/agents/rating.py.
  - Decision logging, N-trading-day settlement and lesson write-back, adapted
    from tradingagents/memory/reflection.py.

